## Phase 18 consumer-list response Fastjson decoder continuation

- Recorded: 2026-10-24
- Code revision: `99f12b9832c3ebca0f9e570c57055cebc375ffd9`
- Fixture: `fixtures/runtime/lookup.json`, SHA-256
  `b3b2efa341e83f40d9b18f345ee175796d8891d84208b2f396f6cf8da162ee33`

The three Core consumer-list response variants previously decoded the DTO via
generic Serde, bypassing the DTO's Java Fastjson adapter. They now call
`ConsumerListByGroupResponseBody::java_decode`, which applies the pinned
`RemotingSerializable.decode` input rules. The invoked DTO differential covers
18 raw inputs plus seven root-shape inputs (25 total). Two Java cases exercise
ordinary trailing text and a second JSON document after raw U+001A. Core sync
and future loopback calls both accept these suffixes and return the prefix
consumer list.

