## Phase 18 typed RPC response Fastjson decoder continuation

- Recorded: 2026-10-24 06:44 UTC
- Code revision: `9a13acb7`
- Fixture: `fixtures/runtime/lookup.json`, SHA-256
  `85c4496ce6e9055da78b4f7624e6713115b90d8c4e7beea60a332c810b5e5bf2`

Audit of Core response decoding found nine typed RPC response variants still
using generic Serde despite pinned 5.5.1 methods calling
`RemotingSerializable.decode`. They now pass the corresponding DTO Java
Fastjson decoder into the shared response helper. The affected types are
QueryAssignmentResponseBody, QueryConsumeTimeSpanBody, LockBatchResponseBody,
GroupList, TopicList, QuerySubscriptionResponseBody, and
ConsumeMessageDirectlyResult. The missing `java_decode` adapters for GroupList
and QuerySubscriptionResponseBody now use the shared Fastjson input layer.

The same audit found controller sync-state, epoch-cache, and election response
bodies going through `serde_json::from_slice`. Their nullable body helper now
uses the shared Java Fastjson decoder, preserving JSON `null` roots as `None`.
The pinned fixture has 14 EOF suffix cases across the seven RPC DTOs and six
across BrokerReplicasInfo, EpochEntryCache, and BrokerMemberGroup. Sync-state,
epoch-cache, and election Core loopback replies also exercise raw U+001A
followed by trailing text.

